  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "section": "narrative",
      "text": "Wellington X HF465 of 12 Operational Training Unit, based at Chipping Warden, was on a daytime training flight when it broke up over Bridgemere, Cheshire. IBCC records the cause as loss of control while descending through cloud. IBCC gives the date as 28 October 1944; the memorial inscription, as transcribed by IWM, reads 20 October 1944. Seven men were aboard and six died.",
      "cites": [
        "C1",
        "C2",
        "C3",
        "C4",
        "C5",
        "C6",
        "C7",
        "C8",
        "C10"
      ],
      "presents_conflict": true
    },
    {
      "section": "narrative",
      "text": "The six who died were Flight Sergeant Leonard Joseph Timperley (pilot, 20), Pilot Officer Cecil Frank Holmes (29), and Sergeants Laurence Edwin Harrison (24), James David Milne (32), Arthur Fred Baker (35) and Ronald Whiteley (23). Timperley is buried at Chester (Blacon) Cemetery. IWM spells the third sergeant's surname Milnes; IBCC and the local history page give Milne. The navigator, Sergeant Douglas Hollis Wilson, survived; IBCC says the aircraft threw him clear, while a local news item says he baled out before it broke up.",
      "cites": [
        "C20",
        "C21",
        "C22",
        "C23",
        "C27",
        "C30",
        "C31",
        "C32",
        "C40",
        "C43",
        "C50",
        "C51",
        "C54",
        "C60",
        "C63",
        "C70",
        "C73",
        "C80",
        "C83",
        "C85"
      ],
      "presents_conflict": true
    },
    {
      "section": "community_connection",
      "text": "The black tablet in a lay-by on the A51 was built by volunteers from donated materials and dedicated in October 2003. The inscription names the crew as RAFVR and lists the survivor separately. A local history page says it came about after Marjorie Harrison, widow of Sergeant Harrison, visited the site in 2000.",
      "cites": [
        "C12",
        "C13",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
