  "custodian_status": "unknown",
  "notes": "Custodian NOT established: no source read says who maintains the memorial. Crewe Town Council (and a Cheshire East Deputy Mayor and Nantwich Mayor) attend the annual service, but that is not shown to be maintenance; the Crewe page was read only via a search excerpt (fetch 404). A Cheshire East cabinet report on war memorials was suggested in search results but its PDF would not parse; unverified whether it lists Bridgemere. Bridgemere is a village outside Crewe; the parish council (likely Doddington and District or Wybunbury) was not checked. IBCC pages for five airmen returned 429; only Timperley's was read, so other airmen's ages/roles rest on the local history page alone (single source), and burial places for them are missing. CWGC not searched directly; no CWGC links. Photo: only the first IWM image used; other three IWM images were not individually verified for credit. The Daily Post story, RAFA Leicester post and Find a Grave links were unreadable (402/403) and not used. ASN is cited from search excerpts only. Memorial reportedly unveiled 28 Oct 2003 per IWM search excerpt; not on the capture, so only 'October 2003' is claimed. The local history page's cause (young pilot, iced wings) is the writer's judgement and not used. Bridgemere pages blhs.co.uk publisher identity assumed from domain; page title said 'All images (c) Philip Coops 2005'. Memorial name field in repo says squadron blank; 12 OTU used."
}
